  "body": "When trying to [implement](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/3863423) the `autocomplete` parsing steps for the new token `webauthn`, I discovered that there are two bugs with the steps I originally proposed that made their way into the spec.\r\n\r\n* If there are two tags like `username webauthn`, the IDL exposed value ends up only being `webauthn` because the algorithm doesn't bother prepending the second token. This is easy to fix: if we find a `webauthn` tag and there is one more tag, we prepend a space and said second token.\r\n* We are supposed to be able to append `webauthn` to any valid `autocomplete` attribute, even for the `Contact` category. However, parsing `Contact` category tokens requires the `category` var to be set to contact, but with `webauthn` it gets set to `Credential`. We can fix this by setting the `category` again with the second token (if it exists). We should also validate that the remaining number of tokens is valid.",
